     "label" -> "T B Method Symbol", "language" -> "en", "paclet" -> 
    "TBMethod", "status" -> "None", "summary" -> 
    "QuantumMetric[{h, velocities}, filling][k] computes the first diagonal \
component of the occupied-band quantum metric at k. QuantumMetric[{h, \
velocities}, filling, {alpha, beta}][k] computes the component specified by \
derivative directions alpha and beta. QuantumMetric[{h, velocities}, q, \
filling, {alpha, beta}][k] uses the symmetrized observable current associated \
with q in the first direction. QuantumMetric[hv, filling, {alpha, beta}][k] \
uses a combined function hv that returns the Hamiltonian and its derivative \
matrices. QuantumMetric[hv, q, filling, {alpha, beta}][k] uses the combined \
Hamiltonian\\[Dash]derivative function and an observable-current insertion.", 
    "synonyms" -> {}, "tabletags" -> {}, "title" -> "QuantumMetric", 
